# Cache headers for the built site.
#
# Netlify defaults every response to `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`.
# suites.dev sits behind Cloudflare, which obeys that header and therefore
# revalidates against the origin on every single request: over a 30 day
# window that produced 140,800 requests with 39 cache hits (0.028%) and
# 775 MB of origin transfer.
#
# Docusaurus content-hashes its build output, so those files can be cached
# permanently; a new build produces new filenames.
#
# Cache-Control is deliberately set on specific paths only and never on /*.
# Netlify merges all matching rules, and its behaviour when the same header
# is set twice is not reliably "most specific wins" - a merged value would
# silently reinstate max-age=0 and make this file a no-op.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
